+# Phase 5A-6: Goal-line censoring, end-of-half FG decision, Q2<2 clock bucket
+
+**Executed by Cowork directly (no Claude Code relay), 2026-09-15.** Code commit
+`21d8de77` (engine, tables, tests); this doc in the follow-up commit.
+All numbers below were measured, not summarised from a session transcript.
+
+## 0. Where 5A-5 left it
+
+After 5A–5A-5 the engine matched reality on plays, drives, yards, explosive plays,
+first downs (total and by type), 3rd-down conversion, penalties and non-offensive
+scoring, and still scored **19.0 pts/team vs 22.4**. 5A-5's actual-side analysis pointed
+at red-zone conversion ("goal-to-go at 1 ≈ 70% TD vs at 8 ≈ 45%; 5-zone table averages
+sharp gradients") and Cowork rejected that as unsupported because the drive-level
+red-zone table (TD given RZ entry 54.1% vs 57.7%) looked close. **That rejection was
+wrong.** 5A-5 had the right region; the mechanism is below.
+
+## 1. Diagnosis — measured per play, not per drive
+
+### 1a. Long-field drives go as far as real ones and still score less
+Conditional on starting inside the own 40 (yl100 ≥ 60), sim vs actual: yards/drive 32.6
+vs 33.1, P(≥60 yds) 24.7% vs 25.9%, plays/drive 6.14 vs 6.03 — but TD share 16% vs 20%.
+Conditional on start 70–75: P(reach RZ) 30.3% vs 27.9% (sim reaches the red zone MORE)
+while P(TD) 16.6% vs 21.1%.
+
+### 1b. Touchdowns by distance (per game, 40-game paired sample, N=500)
+| | sim (pre) | actual |
+|---|---|---|
+| offensive TDs | 3.94 | 4.73 |
+| TDs from ≥ 20 yds out | 0.76 | 1.13 |
+| TDs from < 20 yds out | 3.18 | 3.60 |
+| completions 20+ | 5.44 | 5.93 |
+| completions 40+ | 0.73 | 0.97 |
+| rushes 20+ | 1.29 | 1.30 |
+
+### 1c. TD rate per play by yardline (the decisive table)
+Sim = 6 games × 500 sims with a per-play collector (`engine._DEBUG_YDS`); actual =
+2021–2024 regular season pass/run plays.
+
+| yardline bin | comp TD rate sim (pre) | comp TD rate actual | rush TD rate sim (pre) | rush TD rate actual |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 0–5 | 0.678 | 0.843 | 0.396 | 0.431 |
+| 5–10 | 0.263 | 0.527 | 0.077 | 0.126 |
+| 10–20 | 0.147 | 0.214 | 0.035 | 0.048 |
+| 20–30 | 0.086 | 0.087 | 0.018 | 0.017 |
+| 40–50 | 0.014 | 0.024 | 0.003 | 0.006 |
+| 50–60 | 0.003 | 0.014 | 0.001 | 0.003 |
+
+Per-play yardage distributions pooled over the field match to the third decimal
+(sim completion mean 10.68 vs 10.93; 40–59-yard share 1.4% vs 1.8%; 60+ 0.43% vs 0.45%),
+so the deficit is not the yardage tables' shape in general — it is what happens to the
+drawn gain **near the goal line**.
+
+### 1d. Mechanism: goal-line censoring in pooled zones (classification (i) — a builder bug)
+`tables.py` built each (down, distance, zone) cell's 101 yardage quantiles from
+`yards_gained` as recorded. A scoring play from the 8 records 8 yards, but the play would
+have gained *at least* 8; its true gain is unknown (right-censored at `yardline_100`).
+Pooling censored plays from the 1–3 with plays from the 8–10 into the rz10 zone makes
+the cell's quantiles say "a successful completion here gains 2–3 yards" — true from the
+2, false from the 9. In rz10 33% of completions are censored, in opp20 12%, in midfield
+2.2% (the 40+ tail from the 50–60 is truncated by plays snapped at the 25–35). This is the
+5-zone granularity problem 5A-5 named, with the exact statistical form: censoring, not
+averaging.
+
+## 2. Fixes (all empirical; no constants)
+
+### 2a. Kaplan–Meier yardage quantiles (`tables._km_quantiles`)
+Scoring plays are censored observations (gain ≥ yl); every other play is exact. KM gives
+P(gain ≥ y) for each cell; quantiles come from 1 − S(y). Mass beyond the last uncensored
+gain (the KM plateau) borrows the tail *shape* from the next zone out (rz10 ← opp20's KM
+quantiles ← midfield's; midfield/own zones ← open-field raw gains of the same situation),
+conditional on gain > last observed value; if no reference qualifies, the plateau goes to
+a sentinel (99) that the engine caps at the distance to goal (= reached the end zone).
+Applied to `yds_success_q`, `yds_fail_q`, `yds_all_q` in both pass and rush tables;
+`n_censored` recorded per cell. Sanity test: recorded gains from a uniform-0..9 truth,
+half censored at the 5, give KM q90 = 9 (naive quantile: 7).
+
+Example cell, 1st & long: rz10 successful completions q50/80/90/99 were 8/9/10/10 —
+now 10/18/25/54 (any draw ≥ yl is a TD). opp20: 10/15/17/20 → 10/21/28/58.
+
+### 2b. End-of-half FG on downs 1–3 (new table J, `eoh_fg_decision.parquet`)
+Measured: 0.33 non-4th-down FG attempts/game, 0.29 of them with ≤ 10 s left in the half.
+P(FG | downs 1–3, ≤ 40 s, yl ≤ 50) by (state × seconds × yardline): Q2 or Q4 tied/trailing
+≤ 3 ("fg_useful") 0–3 s: 0.85–0.92 inside the 40, 0.48 from 41–50; 4–6 s: ~0.6 / 0.30;
+7–10 s: 0.09–0.28; 11+ s: ~0. Q4 leading: 0 (kneel). Q4 trailing 4+: ≤ 0.04. Min cell 30,
+pooled-over-yardline fallback. Engine draws the decision before the play call; the
+existing FG execution path runs it.
+
+### 2c. Q2<2 clock bucket (play-call and 4th-down tables)
+Last 2:00 of Q2 was pooled into Q1–3. Measured: pass rate 0.77–0.85 in every score state
+(vs 0.54–0.62 otherwise); 4th-down FG rate in range ~10pp higher. `_clock_bucket_fine`
+now emits "Q2<2"; the engine's play-call and 4th-down bucket strings match; coarse
+fallbacks unchanged.
+
+## 3. Results
+
+### 3a. Paired 40-game sample (same games, seeds, N=500), before → after
+pts/team 19.04 → **21.87**; offensive TDs 3.94 → 4.82 (actual 4.73); TDs from ≥ 20 out
+0.76 → 1.14 (actual 1.13); from < 20 3.18 → 3.68 (actual 3.60); completions 40+ 0.73 →
+0.91 (0.97); FG att 3.45 → 3.32 (actual 3.92); non-4th FG att 0 → 0.16 (actual 0.33);
+P(|m|=3) 8.9% → 8.4%.
+
+### 3b. TD rate per play after the fix
+| yardline bin | comp sim | comp actual | rush sim | rush actual |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 0–5 | 0.876 | 0.843 | 0.498 | 0.431 |
