+
+Reading: the 3.4-point deficit was the goal-line censoring; 2.8 of it is closed and the
+per-season profile now tracks reality (2022–23 within 0.3). The yardage overshoot
+(+5% pass) and the goal-line rush TD overshoot are the same thing seen from two sides:
+KM inside a 40-yard zone still averages a real compression gradient (plays from the 25
+are shorter than plays from the 55 even when the goal line does not bind), and the
+borrowed tail is drawn from the deeper end. The principled next step is KM inside
+10-yard zones with the same tail chain (189k plays support ~120 cells; parent-zone
+fallback below the min cell), not a scale on the output.
+
+## 4. What remains (honest)
+- **Field goals are now the main K1 gap**: 3.3–3.5 att/game vs 3.92. Two measured causes
+  survive: the 4th-down go rate is still 2pp high in range (GOE residual), and the sim
+  reaches "in range with ≤ 40 s left" 1.85 times/game vs 3.32 real — its late-half
+  possessions run 8.2 snaps in the last 2:00 of Q2 vs 9.0 real and 4.5 vs 5.6 in Q4.
+  Timeouts are not modelled; the runoff table absorbs them only on average.
+- Key-number mass (|m|=3 ≈ 8.4% vs 14.5%) follows the FG count and is unchanged.
+- Goal-line rush TD rate overshoots (3b). Candidate refinement: KM within 1–2 / 3–5 /
+  6–10 sub-cells with the same tail chain (data supports it: ~8k plays from the 1–2).
+- Two pre-existing hand constants found while rebuilding tables: `constants.json` carries
+  `p_safety_given_sack_deep 0.85` / `p_safety_given_rush_deep 0.923` (5A-4) that the
+  builder does not produce (a rebuild drops them; restored by hand here), and the engine
+  applies a 0.687 scale to deep sack yardage (5A-4). Both violate the no-constants rule
+  and belong in the builder or out — flagged, not changed.
+- 5A-3 spec tests (go rate ±1.0pp, FG att ±0.15) still fail and are reported red.
+
